-- ── Demo trades ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- 9273 trades across 30 accounts, priced off real daily closes.
-- trade_value is GENERATED ALWAYS — do NOT include it.
-- Chronological per account and instrument, and a SELL never exceeds the position
-- held at that moment, so the derived holdings below are always positive.
--
-- Instruments are joined by ticker rather than carrying a hardcoded instrument_id.
-- The seed does not own these UUIDs: ticker is UNIQUE, so any ticker the running app
-- already resolved at runtime (InstrumentService assigns a random UUID) keeps that row
-- and the insert above is skipped for it. Referencing our own UUID would then point at
-- a row that was never inserted and fail the foreign key, taking startup down with it.
